{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6f406eedc9ccb340b050d5bb23601a9d2d6c00514f35d17bff6c00dfb9c4ec66","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI workflows (GitHub Actions)","key_entities":[".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml",".pre-commit-config.yaml","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","make lint","make typecheck","pre-commit run --all-files","SKIP env var"],"problem_keywords":["ci redundancy","pre-commit","double-run","lint","typecheck","workflow optimization"],"propositions":["The lint and typecheck hooks are executed twice in CI: once as explicit job steps and again via pre-commit run --all-files, causing redundant work.","OSS best practice runs each linter exactly once through a single mechanism rather than double-invoking, as confirmed by pydantic, home-assistant, pandas, scikit-learn, and dmd.","The SKIP environment variable in the pre-commit step should be extended to exclude lint and typecheck hooks in both test.yml and gerrit-verify.yaml workflows.","Local git commits must continue to run lint and typecheck via pre-commit hooks by keeping them in .pre-commit-config.yaml unchanged.","A regression guard test must be added to test_ci_workflow_parity.py to prevent the double-run from silently reoccurring."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787467954090145001,"uuid":"6cb32b5f-e189-4ec3-a043-97c6a3f32631"}